{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirNStability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirNStability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount_unique_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount_unique_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L138-L149","doc":"**The selection, packaged.** Among the three concrete candidates,\nthe bare count is the unique one that both counts modes and is\nn-stable; the Jones value fails stability and the normalised trace\nfails counting. (The Wenzl-sum candidate is covered numerically by\nthe witness; see the module docstring.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.nStable_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.nStable_unique","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L127-L136","doc":"**Uniqueness.** An n-stable, mode-counting functional whose\nsingle-mode value is `1` (the Hoefsmit normalisation: one unknot\ncontributes relative count `1`) is the bare count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.unlinkJones_not_nStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.unlinkJones_not_nStable","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L116-L125","doc":"The Jones value of the n-unlink fails n-stability away from the\nclassical point: comparing cutoffs `1` and `2` forces `δ(q) = 2`,\ni.e. `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.quantumDim_eq_two_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.quantumDim_eq_two_iff","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L89-L114","doc":"`δ(q) = 2` forces the classical point: for `0 < q`,\n`√q + (√q)⁻¹ = 2 ↔ q = 1` (since `δ − 2 = (√q − 1)²/√q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.quantumDim_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.quantumDim_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L84-L87","doc":"The quantum dimension at the classical point: `δ(1) = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.normalizedTrace_not_countsModes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.normalizedTrace_not_countsModes","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L78-L82","doc":"…but content-free: it does not count modes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.normalizedTrace_nStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.normalizedTrace_nStable","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The normalised trace is (vacuously) stable… ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount_nStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount_nStable","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L66-L71","doc":"The bare count is n-stable at every substrate parameter: its\nrelative substrate deviation is identically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount_countsModes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount_countsModes","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The bare count counts modes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.normalizedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.normalizedTrace","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The normalised Markov trace of any identity braid: constant `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.unlinkJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.unlinkJones","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The Jones value of the `n`-unlink: `δ^{n−1}` with quantum dimension\n`δ = √q + (√q)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.bareCount","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The bare disjoint-component count `N(n) = n`, independent of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CountsModes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CountsModes","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L47-L50","doc":"Mode-counting normalisation: at the classical point `q = 1` the\nfunctional counts the vacuum's disjoint components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.NStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.NStable","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirNStability.lean#L38-L45","doc":"n-stability (cutoff admissibility) of a vacuum trace functional\n`F : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ` (value at mode-cutoff `n`, substrate parameter `q`):\nthe relative substrate deviation is independent of the cutoff. In\ndivision-free form: `F m q · F n 1 = F n q · F m 1` for all cutoffs.\nA single-number observable cannot depend on where the mode tower is\ntruncated. ","signatureChunk":0}]}